design:
  - Design B is the default until Daniel answers. He may pick A, B, or C. The design A note gives the amendment.
  - One shared scan reads the raw answer text. It does not depend on JSON.parse success. JSON.parse stays for the review schema only.
  - The input class is every JSON string token of the raw text, at every decoded layer, plus the raw text itself. A JSON string token is a maximal run of characters between two unescaped double quotes. Its decoded form resolves the JSON escape sequences. Each decoded form is a text of the next layer.
  - The scan needs no valid JSON. A malformed, truncated, or duplicated text yields the same tokens as a valid text.
  - The scan is linear in the text length per layer. No path restarts a scan at an opening brace. No call-stack recursion. No depth ceiling.
  - One rule builder serves the raw scan and the decoded scan. Both read the environment at call time.
  - A long pattern name is cut so that the shared suffix stays inside the 500-character cut. The suffix stays byte-identical: the raw answer is refused; no review or raw copy is written.
  - MiniMax calls the scan inside the paid callback, before the success entry. Kimi calls it before parseModelReview and before any record write.
